Nothing in this licence limits any right that the law gives you and that cannot be limited by agreement, including fair dealing under the Copyright Act 1987.

## 14. Governing Law and Severability

This licence is governed by the laws of Malaysia, and the courts of Malaysia have exclusive jurisdiction, subject only to any right the law of your country gives you that cannot be excluded. If any part of this licence is invalid or unenforceable anywhere, it is read down to the minimum extent needed to make it enforceable there, or, if that is not possible, removed there, and the rest stays in full force. A permission that is removed is not replaced by a wider one.
## 15. Version History

1. **Version 1.0** (2026-10-13) was the first version. Release v0.1.0-alpha.1 was published under it, and the source archive of that release contains its text, which continues to govern copies obtained from that release (section 12).
2. **Version 1.1** (2026-10-13) widens the Teaching permission by adding the Teaching With OpenVAPT terms (TEACHING.md): more kinds of teachers, institution virtual machines, and free adaptation of course material. It also adds teaching conditions: TEACHING.md must travel with shared copies, and students under 18 need a parent's or guardian's acceptance. Every other term is unchanged. Anyone holding a version 1.0 copy may instead choose to use that copy under version 1.1 by accepting all of its terms.
3. **Version 1.2** (2026-10-13) adds the definitions of OpenVAPT Material and Credit and a Credit condition (section 5.4): anyone who copies, quotes, shares, adapts or presents OpenVAPT Material must credit OpenVAPT in a reasonable manner, with recommended citations in CITING.md, and CITING.md must travel with shared copies (section 3.4). Using ideas and facts, and running the Software for Own Use, need no Credit, though citation is requested. Every other term is unchanged. Anyone holding a version 1.0 or 1.1 copy may instead choose to use that copy under version 1.2 by accepting all of its terms.

